DecodeLabs – Task 1: Data Cleaning & Preparation

📌 Task Overview
This repository contains the data cleaning pipeline for the DecodeLabs Task 1. The objective was to take a raw e-commerce orders dataset and transform it into a clean, analysis-ready format using Python and Pandas.

📊 Final Dataset Shape
- Rows: 1,200
- Columns: 14

🛠️ Tools Used
- Python 3
- Pandas (Data manipulation)
- NumPy (Numeric operations)
- ReportLab (PDF report generation)

🧹 Data Cleaning Steps (Change Log)
The following operations were performed in `clean_orders.py`:

| Change ID | Description | Impact | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| CR001 | Imputed missing `CouponCode` using the mode | Preserved 1,200 records | Resolved |
| CR002 | Removed duplicate `OrderID`s (kept first) | Achieved 0 duplicate IDs | Resolved |
| CR003 | Standardized `Date` to ISO-8601 (YYYY-MM-DD) | 100% compliant | Resolved |
| CR004 | Title-cased + trimmed text columns | Normalized text data | Resolved |
| CR005 | Rounded `UnitPrice` & `TotalPrice` to 2 decimals | Fixed float artifacts | Resolved |

✅ Verification Checklist
After cleaning, the following assertions were passed:
- Duplicate OrderIDs: 0
- Rows failing ISO-8601 dates: 0
- Nulls in critical fields: 0
- Max decimals in UnitPrice: 2
- Max decimals in TotalPrice: 2

📂 Repository Contents
- `clean_orders.py`: The main Python script containing the cleaning logic, verification assertions, and PDF report generation.
- `Change_log.pdf`: The generated PDF report summarizing the cleaning process and verification metrics.
- `Dataset_Cleaned_Project1.xlsx`: The final cleaned dataset (generated upon running the script).

